WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.070
Let's make Pebble picture friends.

2
00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:06.550
Make a loose pebble dragonfly, bird or turtle on cardboard.

3
00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:09.875
Place and rearrange the stones without glue.

4
00:00:10.255 --> 00:00:12.335
Make this project with a grown-up.

5
00:00:12.715 --> 00:00:15.445
Gather the supplies listed below the video.

6
00:00:15.825 --> 00:00:18.070
Pause whenever you need more time.

7
00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:22.605
An adult chooses stones and keeps the picture on a low stable surface.

8
00:00:22.985 --> 00:00:27.240
Loose stones are not fixed to the card; do not lift it vertically.

9
00:00:28.667 --> 00:00:29.857
Step 1.

10
00:00:30.237 --> 00:00:31.977
Sort your pebble shapes.

11
00:00:32.357 --> 00:00:34.777
Set the cardboard on a flat surface.

12
00:00:35.157 --> 00:00:38.307
Sort stones into long, round and flat shapes.

13
00:00:38.687 --> 00:00:42.626
Pick a large body stone and two to four matching shapes for wings or

14
00:00:42.626 --> 00:00:42.907
legs.

15
00:00:43.287 --> 00:00:44.667
Grown-up help.

16
00:00:45.047 --> 00:00:47.687
Check every stone and the working surface.

17
00:00:49.167 --> 00:00:50.347
Step 2.

18
00:00:50.727 --> 00:00:52.407
Imagine the picture.

19
00:00:52.787 --> 00:00:55.432
Choose a dragonfly, bird or turtle.

20
00:00:55.812 --> 00:00:59.543
Lightly draw its shape on the card, or point to where the body and

21
00:00:59.543 --> 00:01:00.342
head will go.

22
00:01:00.722 --> 00:01:02.362
Leave a clear border.

23
00:01:02.742 --> 00:01:04.122
Grown-up help.

24
00:01:04.502 --> 00:01:07.022
Draw a simple outline if helpful.

25
00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:09.845
Step 3.

26
00:01:10.225 --> 00:01:11.865
Place the big shapes.

27
00:01:12.245 --> 00:01:15.655
Put the largest stones down first for the body and head.

28
00:01:16.035 --> 00:01:19.460
Leave space around them for wings, legs or a tail.

29
00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:22.230
Turn the stones until they sit flat.

30
00:01:22.610 --> 00:01:23.990
Grown-up help.

31
00:01:24.370 --> 00:01:26.045
Help with heavy stones.

32
00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:28.650
Step 4.

33
00:01:29.030 --> 00:01:30.805
Add the little details.

34
00:01:31.185 --> 00:01:34.705
Add broad wing stones or short leg stones beside the body.

35
00:01:35.085 --> 00:01:39.406
Draw tiny details such as eyes on the card near the stones instead of

36
00:01:39.406 --> 00:01:40.640
using small loose pieces.

37
00:01:42.167 --> 00:01:43.342
Step 5.

38
00:01:43.722 --> 00:01:45.197
Tell its story.

39
00:01:45.577 --> 00:01:48.777
Give the creature a name and describe where it lives.

40
00:01:49.157 --> 00:01:51.562
Keep the board flat while admiring it.

41
00:01:51.942 --> 00:01:55.897
Photograph the picture before returning the stones to their storage box.

42
00:01:56.277 --> 00:01:57.657
Grown-up help.

43
00:01:58.037 --> 00:02:00.492
Help clear the stones individually.

44
00:02:02.001 --> 00:02:04.916
Here are three ideas for your finished project.

45
00:02:05.296 --> 00:02:08.846
These example pictures were made with artificial intelligence.

46
00:02:09.226 --> 00:02:11.246
Your creation can look different.

47
00:02:11.626 --> 00:02:14.831
Remove stones one by one and reuse the card.

48
00:02:15.211 --> 00:02:19.308
Keep flat and out of reach of younger children and pets, or save a

49
00:02:19.308 --> 00:02:19.601
picture.

50
00:02:19.981 --> 00:02:20.971
Well done.

51
00:02:21.351 --> 00:02:23.781
Take a moment to enjoy what you made.

